---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import verified from '../../../../../public/equipment/09-01/verification.json';
import geom from '../../../../../public/equipment/09-01/geometry-check.json';
import metrics from '../../../../../public/equipment/09-01/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/09-01/',doc='https://www.gamry.com/assets/Uploads-v2/Reference-600%2BOperators-Manual-v6.5.pdf',legacy='https://www.gamry.com/support-2/legacy-devices/reference-600plus-legacy/';
const refs=[['front',52,'Front panel','Manual p. 52 shows the foil-colored front, four status LEDs and vertical DB25 cell connector. No screen or manual method controls.'],['rear',55,'Rear connections','Manual pp. 55–56 show the +24 V jack and rocker, USB-B, fan grilles, BNC monitor ports and chassis ground. Only the rocker operates here.'],['side',1,'Side and enclosure','The manual cover shows the shallower end wraps, metal side and dark front bezel; reference scale from legacy product specs. Port offsets and bezel profiles are inferred.'],['work',47,'Cell cable and dummy board','Manual p. 47 confirms lead colors and the WE/WS pairing. Commercial calibration-board imagery is on pp. 40 and 42. Our blue-gray passive RC board is original, rather than a reproduction of either Gamry accessory.']];
const scope=Object.keys(import.meta.glob('../09-04/simulator.astro')).length>0;
---
<Layout pageTitle="Gamry Reference 600+" subtitle="" description="Run electrochemical impedance and cyclic voltammetry against a passive electronic dummy cell." wide={true}>
<article id="rx" class="equipment">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-01/">← Equipment 09-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#references">References</a><a href="#verification">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="rx-head"><p class="eq-meta">09-01 / Electrochemical characterization / Electronic calibration bench</p><h2>Gamry Reference 600+</h2><p>The legacy upright Reference 600+ with the standard shielded 985-00150 cell cable, not the successor Reference 620. A passive 1 kΩ ∥ 1 µF dummy circuit is already wired. Run EIS to find the −45° shoulder, then switch to the capacitor CV example to see the current flip when the ramp reverses.</p></header>
<div class="rx-grid">
<section class="rx-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the instrument</h3><div class="rx-bar" id="rx-views">{['Bench','Front','Rear','Side','Work'].map(v=><button type="button" data-view={v.toLowerCase()}>{v}</button>)}<button id="rx-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="rx-canvas" aria-label="Orbitable Reference 600+ and passive dummy cell"></canvas>
<p id="rx-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Click the DB25 plug to disconnect it, a lead on the dummy board to open its circuit, or the rear rocker to cycle power. Drag to orbit; scroll or pinch to zoom. Bench resets the view.</p></section>
<section class="rx-card"><h3>02 · Set up and acquire</h3><form id="rx-config">
<div class="rx-bar"><button type="button" id="power">Power off</button><button type="button" id="cable">Unplug DB25</button>{['WE','WS','RE','CE'].map(k=><button type="button" data-lead={k}>{k} ✓</button>)}</div>
<div class="rx-fields">
<label>Method<select name="mode"><option value="eis">Potentiostatic EIS</option><option value="cv">Cyclic voltammetry</option></select></label>
<label>Sample ID<input name="sampleId" value="rc-reference-01" required maxlength="96"/></label>
<label>Dummy cell<select name="pure"><option value="false">Rs + (Rp ∥ C)</option><option value="true">Pure capacitor</option></select></label>
<label>Rs (Ω)<input type="number" name="rsOhm" min="0" max="100000" step="any" value="0"/></label>
<label>Rp (Ω)<input type="number" name="rpOhm" min="1" max="10000000" step="any" value="1000"/></label>
<label>C (µF)<input type="number" name="cF" min="0" max="10000" step="any" value="1"/></label>
<label>Point budget<input type="number" name="n" min="5" max="301" value="81"/></label>
<label>Current range (mA)<input type="number" name="currentRangeA" min=".001" max="600" value="6" step="any"/></label>
<label data-mode="eis">Start (Hz)<input type="number" name="fLo" min=".01" max="100000" step="any" value="1"/></label>
<label data-mode="eis">Stop (Hz)<input type="number" name="fHi" min=".01" max="100000" step="any" value="100000"/></label>
<label data-mode="eis">AC drive (mV RMS)<input type="number" name="vRms" min=".1" max="50" step="any" value="10"/></label>
<label data-mode="cv" hidden>Vertices ± (V)<input type="number" name="halfSpanV" min=".005" max="1" step="any" value=".2"/></label>
<label data-mode="cv" hidden>Scan rate (V/s)<input type="number" name="scanVps" min=".00001" max="10" step="any" value=".1"/></label>
</div>
<div class="rx-bar"><button type="submit" class="rx-run" id="run">Run experiment</button><button type="button" id="presetEis">Reset EIS</button><button type="button" id="presetCv">Capacitor CV</button></div>
</form><p id="rx-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready: power, cable, and required leads are connected.</p></section></div>
<section class="rx-card"><h3>03 · Read the result</h3><p id="rx-result" role="status">No data acquired.</p>
<div class="rx-bar"><button id="json" disabled>Result JSON</button><button id="csv" disabled>Points CSV</button><button id="wave" disabled>CV voltage waveform JSON</button></div>
<svg id="rx-chart" viewBox="0 0 700 245" role="img" aria-label="Impedance or cyclic voltammetry plot"></svg>
<details><summary>Individual readings, signs and overload flags</summary><div class="rx-table"><table><thead id="rx-rows-head"></thead><tbody id="rx-rows"></tbody></table></div></details></section>
<section id="references"><h3>Illustrated references</h3><p>These four images are original renders, not photographs or OEM CAD. The linked pages give the actual panel photographs and accessory documentation. Gamry’s <a href={legacy}>legacy equipment record</a> identifies the selected revision family and successor.</p>
<div class="rx-refs">{refs.map(([v,p,title,desc])=><figure><img src={a+v+'.webp'} width="600" height="398" loading="lazy" alt={'Original 3D view: '+title}/><figcaption><strong>{title}.</strong> {desc} <a href={doc+'#page='+p}>View the manual photo or figure</a>.</figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="rx-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value and conditions</th><th>Use / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Instrument envelope W × H × D</td><td>Nominal 90 × 190 × 270 mm; manual states a maximum of 100 × 200 × 300 mm</td><td>Geometry. <a href={legacy}>Legacy product specs</a>; <a href={doc+'#page=77'}>988-00006 Rev 6.6 appendix A, p. 77</a>. No production CAD or measurement.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cell cable</td><td>985-00150; 60 cm nominal; DB25 with five 2 mm plugs and one pin jack</td><td>Configuration and connection topology. <a href={doc+'#page=47'}>Rev 6.6 p. 47</a>. Visual path and board dimensions are inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Power and links</td><td>External +24 V DC supply, USB 2.0, rear panel rocker</td><td>Ports and state. <a href={doc+'#page=55'}>Rev 6.6 pp. 55–58</a>. No firmware or bus emulation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hardware ranges</td><td>10 µHz–5 MHz EIS at appropriate fixture/range; ±22 V counter compliance; >±600 mA amplifier output</td><td>Context, not simulated extremes; accuracy depends on load and cable. <a href={legacy}>Legacy product specs</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Simulation operating limits</td><td>0.01 Hz–100 kHz; 0.1–50 mV RMS; CV ±5 mV to ±1 V; 0.01 mV/s–10 V/s; 1 µA–600 mA full scale</td><td>Declared software bounds, not a claim about hardware current ranges or calibration.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>Model and input/output contract</h3>
<p>The subject is a passive electronic calibration circuit. WE and WS share RC-HI; CE and RE share RC-LO. Voltage is WS minus RE; positive current enters the dummy load at RC-HI. Disconnecting any required lead, DB25 or power rejects the acquisition. Orange Counter Sense and floating ground are parked open, not part of this potentiostatic fixture.</p>
<p><b>EIS.</b> The small-signal linear circuit gives Z(ω) = Rs + Rp/(1 + jωRpC); pure capacitor mode uses 1/(jωC). RMS current is Vrms/|Z|. A frequency point is flagged and its measured impedance withheld when peak current exceeds the selected full scale. This is a readout-overload model, not amplifier clipping. Fit unflagged points by linear regression of ω/(−Im Z) versus ω², invert for Rp and C, then estimate Rs from Re Z and report a complex RMS residual. Narrow sweeps without sufficient frequency/phase coverage suppress the fit.</p>
<p><b>CV.</b> Apply one symmetric triangular ramp from −V to +V and back at constant |dV/dt|, starting from DC steady state. For finite Rs and C the branch voltage obeys dv/dt = ((Rp/(Rs+Rp))E − v)/(C(Rs∥Rp)) and is integrated exactly per linear segment. If Rs=0, I = E/Rp + C dE/dt; for a pure capacitor only I = C dE/dt remains. The point at the vertex is the forward-limit value. Point budget rounds down to equal legs plus their shared vertex. No redox chemistry, diffusion, corrosion, nonlinearity, cable compensation or measurement uncertainty is modeled.</p>
<p>Exports carry specimen and contact IDs, configuration in SI units, parent/measurement revisions, overload flags and simulated provenance. Result revision does not change the dummy circuit. A CV-only voltage export uses a uniform time base; frequency-domain EIS data are not time samples. <a href={a+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a> · <a href={a+'example-eis.json'}>EIS example</a> · <a href={a+'example-cv-waveform.json'}>CV waveform example</a> · <a href={a+'handoff-verification.json'}>09-04 handoff evidence</a>. The scope solver acquired 33 triggered samples from the example at 10 Sa/s, without clipping and with the WS_minus_RE contact preserved. {scope && <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/">Open the 09-04 oscilloscope</a>}</p>
</section>
<section id="verification"><h3>Verification notebook</h3><p>Reference values were set before code. These checks establish model arithmetic and approximate enclosure scale, not equivalence to a measured 600+ spectrum.</p><div class="rx-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance / unit</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>{verified.map(r=><tr><td>{r.id}</td><td>{typeof r.expected==='string'?r.expected:Object.entries(r.expected).map(([k,v])=>k+' '+Number(v.toPrecision(9))).join('; ')}</td><td>{typeof r.actual==='string'?r.actual:Object.entries(r.actual).map(([k,v])=>k+' '+Number(v.toPrecision(9))).join('; ')}</td><td>{r.tolerance??'exact'} {r.units}</td><td>{r.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}{geom.checks.map(g=><tr><td>Geometry · {g.axis}</td><td>{g.referenceMm} mm</td><td>{g.actualMm} mm</td><td>±{g.toleranceMm} mm</td><td>{g.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>3D and integration files</h3><p><a href={a+'reference-600-plus.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'model.py'}>Editable Blender generator</a> + <a href={a+'pack.py'}>mesh packer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>XR interaction anchors</a> · <a href={a+'solver.mjs'}>Headless study and actions</a> · <a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared checks</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Numerical evidence</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-check.json'}>Geometry check</a>.</p><p>{metrics.triangles.toLocaleString('en-US')} triangles, {metrics.drawCalls} material primitives, {Math.round(metrics.bytes/1024)} KiB. The same state reducer drives screen, model and exports. Optional immersive WebXR uses meter scale and controller ray selection. Physical headset behavior and performance are unverified.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
